@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] one-active-writer
At most one claim in a holding state (pending, active, releasing, uncertain) MAY contain overlapping items:
scopes overlap with ancestors and descendants, paths and prefixes when one contains the other. The overlap
check and the reservation MUST happen in one database transaction of the single service process. Resolving or
reconciling an ended claim MUST NOT return it to a holding state while another claim holds an overlapping item.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] verified-lfs-binding
A claim MUST become active only after the service read every declared LFS lock on the remote with the
recorded path, ID and the claimant's registered account, and re-checked the base against the target branch.
Ownership MUST come from the claim, never from an LFS account match.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] fail-closed
An unreachable or unverifiable service, LFS server or Git remote MUST refuse grants, activation and protected
checks. Every protected check MUST re-verify the task's active claims live (each LFS lock's path, ID and owner on
the remote, and the base against the target branch); stored state alone MUST NOT pass it. A restarted service
MUST refuse grants until a reconcile pass completed. Unprotected changes MAY pass.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:safety] proven-own-unlock
Only locks proven created by the claim's own attempt (reported created, or absent from its intent snapshot,
owned by the claimant and not attributable to another claim's attempt by the same account) MAY be marked for
unlock; a coordinator MAY hand a pre-existing lock only to a live claim that never attempted that path. Unknown
outcomes MUST stay uncertain and keep the reservation until the lock is seen or the settle interval (longer than
a lock request can stay in flight) passed with no lock, or a coordinator resolves it; a retry MUST NOT replace
an unsettled attempt before then. A lock in the intent
snapshot MUST NOT be adopted or unlocked, whatever its account.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:correctness] release-only-on-merge-or-cancel
A claim MUST be released only by a merge whose revision is reachable from the target branch, an explicit
owner cancellation recording preserved or discarded changes, an aborted acquisition, or a recorded
coordinator recovery. Pushes, failed pushes and expired heartbeats MUST NOT release or transfer a claim.
